Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(pricing):=20GEO-004=20=E2=80=94=20New=20Yo?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rk=20is=20priced=20in=20New=20York?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes GC-024. Every New York surface published the Ontario bands in Canadian
dollars while content/geo/markets.ts said, in three places, that the bands are
Toronto facts and appear on no page as local United States facts.

Three USD bands (owner decision D6): screen and recoat $2.00–$3.25, full sand
and finish $4.00–$6.25, new install $9.25–$15.00. The crossing and the travel
are inside them. The exchange basis and the travel allowance are published
nowhere — a rate is stale within a day and an uplift is one division from the
margin — and are recorded once in docs/GEO_SOURCE_MAP.md D6.

Four surfaces were handing Buffalo a Canadian price: the site-wide FAQ, the
service cards, areaToMarkdown, and CommercialHeadTermRail, which built its own
price strings and rendered 'refinishing in Buffalo … $4.75–$7.50' in content on
26 pages. Measured after: 0 Canadian figures on any New York page or twin.

One rate card per country, not per corridor — eleven sentences promising one
rate card everywhere were rescoped to 'within a country', so the promise and
the prices agree. Registry ids are additive; no existing id changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
